# Get started

This repository is a Dart pub workspace named **zonai**. Use the pinned Flutter/Dart SDK via **FVM** so versions match the team and `pubspec.yaml` constraints.

## Prerequisites

- [Git](https://git-scm.com/)
- [FVM](https://fvm.app/) (Flutter Version Management)

## 1. Clone and submodules

```bash
git clone <repository-url> zonai
cd zonai
git submodule update --init --recursive
```

The **raindrop** ORM lives under `libs/raindrop` as a submodule, pinned to the **`zonai`** branch on the fork [mrgnhnt96/raindrop](https://github.com/mrgnhnt96/raindrop). The original project is [wolfenrain/raindrop](https://github.com/wolfenrain/raindrop); inside the submodule, `origin` is the fork and `upstream` is wolfenrain. The fork’s repo root is a separate Dart workspace; checking out only `packages/` avoids a conflict with this monorepo’s workspace resolution (“stray pubspec”). Run:

```bash
./tool/setup_raindrop_submodule.sh
```

Run this after clone, or whenever `libs/raindrop` looks like a full upstream checkout again (for example after `git submodule update` without sparse checkout). The script initializes the submodule if needed and applies the sparse-checkout rules.

## 2. Flutter / Dart SDK (FVM)

This project pins a Flutter version under `.fvm/` (see `.fvm/fvm_config.json`). Install and use it from the repo root:

```bash
fvm install
fvm use
```

If `fvm use` reports the version is already installed, you can skip `fvm install`.

## 3. Dependencies

Resolve the whole workspace from the repository root:

```bash
fvm dart pub get
```

## 4. App configs and env flavors

When you work on a Zonai app (e.g. `apps/playground`), you can maintain multiple **app config** Dart files and **`.env`** files for different targets (dev, staging, prod). Pass `--flavor <name>` to select which config file and which `.env.<flavor>` file to use. Env keys are baked into worker executables at compile time via `String.fromEnvironment`, not read from disk at runtime.

See **[config-and-env-flavors.md](config-and-env-flavors.md)** for file precedence, compile flow, worker outputs, and examples.

For production builds and server deploys, pass **`--release`** so worker executables are compiled without `--enable-asserts`. See **[release-mode.md](release-mode.md)**.

To change which address the HTTP server listens on, set **`host`** and **`port`** in `zonai.yaml` or pass **`--host`** / **`--port`** to `serve`. See **[server-binding.md](server-binding.md)**.

## 5. Collection operations

Each database collection needs an operations class that turns API requests into SQL. Add one Dart file per collection under `lib/src/operations` (or your `operationsPath`). See **[operations.md](operations.md)** for layout, `CollectionOperations`, auth mixins, and custom operations.

## 6. Access rules

Each collection needs rules that decide who may read and write data. Add collection- and record-level Dart files under `lib/src/rules` (or your `rulesPath`). See **[rules.md](rules.md)** for the two-level model, JWT checks, auth rules, and examples.

## 7. Extensions

To run Dart hooks around creates, updates, deletes, and auth events (side effects, emails, related row updates), add one extension file per collection under `lib/src/extensions` (or your `extensionsPath`). See **[extensions.md](extensions.md)** for hook methods, `get` / `mutate` / `email` APIs, and examples.

For session token refresh (`POST /auth/refresh`), see **[auth.md](auth.md)**.

## 8. Rate limiting

To throttle API traffic per client IP and collection, add Dart files under `lib/src/rate_limit` (or your `rateLimitPath`). See **[rate-limiting.md](rate-limiting.md)** for policy methods, defaults, and examples.

## 9. Optional checks

- Run CLI package tests:

  ```bash
  fvm dart test apps/cli
  ```

- **Infra / env tooling** (`pnv`) is declared in `support/infra`; use that package’s workflows when you work on infrastructure.

## Troubleshooting

- **`Found a pubspec.yaml ... stray`** near `libs/raindrop`: run `./tool/setup_raindrop_submodule.sh` so the raindrop root `pubspec.yaml` is not present beside `packages/`.
- **SDK version errors**: ensure you are using `fvm dart` / `fvm flutter`, not a mismatched global SDK.
